  "description": "BEMBII crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C112 H97 Lu5 N2 O23,3(C5 H5 N1). From the CIF bond table, Lu1 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu2 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu3 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors; Lu4 (Lu) has 7 O neighbors; Lu5 (Lu) has 8 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 10 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a network with cycles with three-dimensional metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.400-4.964 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 87.13-163.80°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula [Lu5(OH)5(L4)2(DBM)6]. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 5 OH (explicit grouped unit in article formula).",
